lina: Putting this here: NextStarter-lite (Next.js edge + LlamaIndex adapter) is intermittently failing our eval harness with truncated outputs. Repro in local dev noted.

kevin: Thanks. Initial hunch: auth refresh race + edge runtime env differences.

lina: Fetch handler in starter looks like:```js
export const runtime = 'edge';
export default async function handler(req) {
  const r = await fetch(process.env.REDWOOD_API_URL + '/v1/chat', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY}` },
    body: JSON.stringify({ input: req.json().input })
  });
  return new Response(await r.text(), { status: r.status });
}
```

ashley: Two things: edge mode on some platforms doesn't expose process.env the same way, and the starter pins SDK 0.12.0. We fixed an auth refresh bug in 0.12.3.

tom_sre: CI harness currently flags any non-200 as hard fail. We should make it resilient to transient 401s due to refresh and retry a couple times with backoff.

kevin: Plan: bump SDK in starter to 0.12.3, add a small guard that errors clearly when auth header missing, and add a short README blurb "Edge runtime note". Also add an msw-based integration test that simulates token expiry.

lina: I'll open the PR to bump and add the guard. Will include minimal repro steps in README so users aren't blocked.

ci-bot: Created issue #1599: "nextstarter-lite: auth refresh race on edge causes eval harness truncation" assigned to lina  https://issues.redwood/1599

ashley: After PR merges, I'll re-run the eval harness and mark CI job non-flaky. :ship:
